well, now that the "experts" have revealed themselves, what the average
player wants to know is (we already sort of suspected that you couldn't
currently port save files):

could it be possible in a future version of the game that save (and
related type) files be sufficiently abstracted so that i could play
_my_ saved game on any nethack game processor?

in a related sense, shouldn't i be able to "design" a level (perhaps
using an interactive dungeon compiler) that could work like bones in
any standard dungeon?  and, i shouldn't need access to the playground
to make the game aware of my designer level.

okay, this might mean encoding config and version tokens into the save
file along with using a universal compression scheme and what have you,
but surely such a thing is possible, no?

let's assume that we can sacrifice some file size in order to achieve
this end and that we're restricted to dungeons that are "configured"
the same (default) way.  what say you to this?

